!
! Rain in tenths of a millimetre as hundredths of an inch
! (weatherglass_model.h WG1), in Trebago: an inch is 25.4 mm, 254 tenths,
! so rain * 100 / 254 = rain * 50 / 127, an exact reduced rational, never
! rounded (127 tenths is exactly 50, half an inch). The domain is
! 0 .. 99999 tenths (9999.9 mm, past any rain measured in a day): ok is 1
! inside it and 0 outside, and the answer is divided by it, so a negative
! or larger amount is a division by zero, refused, where rain.kron
! answers: held.
trebago rain
  in  rain(n)
  out inch(n)
  var ok(n)
  ok(i) = min(1, max(0, rain(i) + 1)) * min(1, max(0, 100000 - rain(i)))
  inch(i) = rain(i) * 50 / 127 / ok(i)
end
